            <ArticleTitle>[Anti-angina effectiveness of sustak and obzidan in the acute period of myocardial infarct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sustak and obsidan were given separately and in combination to 99 patients with acute myocardial infarction and frequent attacks of angina pectoris. With the use of these agents the attacks of angina pectoris were very rare. The course of the disease and the prognosis were more favourable in the group of patients treated with anti-anginal agents than in the control group (100 patients).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
